WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.494
Most product demos fake the interface or hide behind jump

00:00:03.494 --> 00:00:04.057
cuts.

00:00:04.057 --> 00:00:07.057
This one is different: every screen, click, and field comes

00:00:07.057 --> 00:00:10.417
from a real browser session timed to the narration.

00:00:10.597 --> 00:00:12.501
Start a new launch workspace.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.193
Give it a clear name, choose the campaign template, and

00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:17.502
mark it as priority so the team knows this work

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:19.368
should lead the queue.

00:00:19.548 --> 00:00:23.327
Create the project and Orbit updates the workspace immediately.

00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:26.367
The new launch plan appears with its template and priority

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.848
state intact.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.752
Now search the live project list, narrow the records to

00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:33.572
the one you need, and reopen the project without breaking

00:00:33.572 --> 00:00:35.256
the narrated flow.

00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:38.443
Inside the project, add the next concrete task.

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:41.547
Name the campaign review, assign it to Jordan, and save

00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:45.411
it so ownership and progress stay visible in one place.

00:00:45.591 --> 00:00:48.503
Move to automations and enable status alerts.

00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:51.372
From here, review and blocked changes can reach the project

00:00:51.372 --> 00:00:54.762
channel without someone manually chasing every update.

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:58.370
Then open the team workspace, invite Mina, choose the editor

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.882
role, and send access.

00:00:59.882 --> 00:01:02.870
The demo uses disposable data, but the actions are the

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.183
same semantic controls a real product exposes.

00:01:06.363 --> 00:01:10.754
That was one continuous browser take: creation, configuration, search, task

00:01:10.754 --> 00:01:13.459
assignment, automation, and collaboration.

00:01:13.459 --> 00:01:18.109
Narova adds narration, word-synced captions, scene-aware framing, and evidence for

00:01:18.109 --> 00:01:21.919
every important step, ready for a walkthrough, onboarding video, or

00:01:21.919 --> 00:01:23.352
sales demo.
